{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-5","title":"prop:dc-ch3-2-5","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":161,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#prop:dc-ch3-2-5","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-exist]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-chart-family]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-family]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"prop:dc-ch3-2-5","line":448,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[local existence/uniqueness of geodesics]\n  \\label{prop:dc-ch3-2-5}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-2-5-exist, lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique, lem:dc-ch3-2-5-chart-family, lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-family}\n  \\dcref{ch3:2.5}\n  Given $p\\in M$, there exist an open set $V\\subset M$ with $p\\in V$, numbers\n  $\\delta>0$, $\\varepsilon_1>0$, and a $C^\\infty$ map\n  $$\n  \\gamma:(-\\delta,\\delta)\\times\\mathcal{U}\\to M,\\quad\\mathcal{U}=\\{(q,v);\\ q\\in V,\\ v\\in T_qM,\\ |v|<\\varepsilon_1\\},\n  $$\n  such that $t\\mapsto\\gamma(t,q,v)$, $t\\in(-\\delta,\\delta)$, is the unique geodesic\n  passing through $q$ with velocity $v$ at $t=0$, for each $q\\in V$ and each\n  $v\\in T_qM$ with $|v|<\\varepsilon_1$.\n\\end{proposition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[local existence/uniqueness of geodesics] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a64632d6368332d322d35\